.TH GNULTE 1 "2026-09-12" "GNULTE 8.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
GNULTE \- GNU LAN Network Testing Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B GNULTE
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GNULTE
is an interactive tool for running authorised network tests on networks you own
or have explicit written permission to test. It applies kernel-level traffic
shaping (\fBtc netem\fR) and ARP spoofing (\fBarpspoof\fR) to simulate network
degradation against target devices, so you can observe how applications behave
under poor network conditions.
.PP
During monitoring GNULTE pings each target once per second and shows a live
dashboard; spoof processes are watched and restarted automatically if they die.
.PP
On first run (and whenever versioned safety documents change) GNULTE shows the
legal and safety documents and requires explicit acknowledgment before any
network-impacting operation can run. There is no flag that bypasses this.
Unauthorised network interference is illegal in most jurisdictions; you are
solely responsible for your actions. See SAFETY.md, DISCLAIMER.md,
AUTHORIZED-USE.md and NETWORK-TESTING.md (installed under
.I share/doc/gnulte
when installed via installer.sh).
.SH SCOPE
IPv4 only. Traffic control is applied through
.B tc
filters that match only the selected target devices; unrelated devices on the
interface are not shaped. On exit the original
.B net.ipv4.ip_forward
value and the previous root qdisc are restored, only the
.B arpspoof
instances GNULTE started are terminated, and the gateway's ARP entry is
broadcast so target caches re-converge quickly.
.B \-\-capture
stores everything a target sends unencrypted — treat the resulting
.B .pcap
as a secret.
.B Warning:
every network-impacting operation (ARP MITM, capture, impairment, active deep
scanning) requires deliberate confirmation; a \fBNo\fR answer cancels the
operation before anything touches the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-t, \-\-target " IP
Target one or more comma-separated IP addresses.
.TP
.BI "\-m, \-\-mac " MAC
Resolve and target a device by MAC address.
.TP
.BI "\-r, \-\-range " CIDR
Target every host in a CIDR range (e.g. 192.168.1.0/24). Your own IP and any
whitelisted IPs are excluded automatically.
.TP
.BI "\-w, \-\-whitelist " IP
Exclude IP(s) from a range test (comma-separated).
.TP
.BI "\-l, \-\-latency " MS
Base delay in milliseconds (default 2000).
.TP
.BI "\-j, \-\-jitter " MS
Random delay variation in milliseconds (default 500).
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-loss " PERCENT
Percentage of packets to drop (default 0).
.TP
.BI "\-d, \-\-duplicate " PERCENT
Percentage of packets to duplicate (default 0).
.TP
.BI "\-e, \-\-reorder " PERCENT
Percentage of packets to reorder (default 0).
.TP
.BI "\-b, \-\-bandwidth " KBPS
Bandwidth cap in kbit/s; 0 means unlimited (default 0).
.TP
.BI "\-\-profile " NAME
Use a preset profile: gaming, streaming, voip, web, extreme, throttle.
.TP
.B \-\-random
Vary parameters randomly during the run.
.TP
.BI "\-\-duration " SECONDS
Automatically stop after N seconds.
.TP
.BI "\-\-export " CSV
Append per-second ping results to a CSV file.
.TP
.B \-\-scan
Deep scan selected targets (ports, OS detection, hostname) using nmap.
.TP
.B \-\-quick
Use a fast ARP-only scan.
.TP
.BI "\-\-capture " FILE
Capture the target's traffic with \fBtcpdump\fR to FILE (pcap format) while the
test runs, so you can later inspect what the applications actually experienced.
.TP
.B \-\-dupcheck
Scan the LAN for duplicate IP addresses / ARP conflicts (an IP answered by more
than one MAC), then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Skip interactive configuration prompts (requires explicit flags).
.TP
.B \-\-no-banner
Skip the branding/boot screen and start plainly. Alias:
.B \-\-minimal.
.TP
.BI "\-\-save\-profile " NAME
Save the current parameter set as a custom profile.
.TP
.BI "\-\-log\-mode " MODE
Output verbosity: normal, simple, or quiet.
.TP
.BI "\-\-verbosity " LEVEL
Console complexity: easy (plain-language explanations), normal, or expert
(shows every raw command and confirms before each spoof/shaping step).
.TP
.BI "\-\-theme " NAME
Colour theme: classic, hacker, ocean, sunset, highcontrast, mono, or custom.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the interactive settings app (theme preview, verbosity, log mode).
.TP
.BI "\-\-log\-file " FILE
Write a session log to FILE.
.TP
.B \-\-config
Edit the user configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI "\-h, \-\-help"
Show help text and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gnulte/acceptance
Safety-policy acceptance record (data file, versioned via SAFETY_POLICY_VERSION).
.TP
.I ~/.gnulte.conf
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.gnulte_profiles.conf
Custom saved profiles.
.TP
.I gnulte-report-<timestamp>/
Post-test reports containing report.txt and report.html with latency graphs.
.PP
The legacy marker \fI~/.gnulte_accepted\fR is no longer read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success (including normal Ctrl+C cleanup).
.PP
non-zero on configuration failure, interrupted setup, or missing dependencies.
.SH SECURITY
Root is required only for arpspoof, tc, and sysctl operations; GNULTE elevates
those via sudo. Prefer running GNULTE as your normal user rather than as root.
Only ever use on networks you own or have written permission to test. Report
vulnerabilities per SECURITY.md (privately, without credentials or captures).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arpspoof (8),
.BR tc (8),
.BR arp-scan (1),
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR nmap (1)